{"title":"Career Roadmap · Public Prosecutor","role":"Public Prosecutor","summary":"A Public Prosecutor (PP) represents the State in criminal proceedings and conducts prosecution on behalf of the government. The role involves presenting evidence, examining and cross-examining witnesses, making legal submissions, handling criminal cases and assisting the court in reaching a legally sound decision.","facts":{"Current degree":"Law - LLB / BA LLB / BBA LLB / B.Com LLB / B.Sc LLB (Integrated)","Course":"Criminal Law"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Public Prosecutor (PP) represents the State in criminal proceedings and conducts prosecution on behalf of the government. The role involves presenting evidence, examining and cross-examining witnesses, making legal submissions, handling criminal cases and assisting the court in reaching a legally sound decision."},{"type":"p","text":"The career is particularly suited to students who enjoy:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Criminal law"},{"text":"Courtroom advocacy"},{"text":"Evidence analysis"},{"text":"Legal research"},{"text":"Public service"},{"text":"Oral argument"},{"text":"Investigation-related legal issues"},{"text":"Procedural law"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"completing an LLB does not automatically make someone a Public Prosecutor. Appointment eligibility, required practice experience, recruitment examinations and selection procedures vary according to the relevant State/Central authority and the applicable law."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Class 12","LLB / Integrated Law Degree","Criminal Law + Criminal Procedure + Evidence","Law Internship","Enrollment / Professional Qualification as Applicable","Practice as Advocate","Criminal Litigation Experience","Eligibility for Relevant Recruitment / Appointment","Public Prosecutor / Assistant Public Prosecutor","Senior Public Prosecutor","Government Law Officer / Senior Prosecution Role","Directorate / Leadership Roles in Prosecution"]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact entry route differs between jurisdictions and posts. Some prosecution positions may be recruited through competitive examinations, while others involve eligibility-based appointments."}]},{"heading":"What You Learn During LLB","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Legal Foundations"},{"type":"h","text":"Core Subjects"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Constitutional Law"},{"text":"Law of Torts"},{"text":"Contract Law"},{"text":"Legal Methods"},{"text":"Legal Language"},{"text":"Legal History"},{"text":"Legal Reasoning"},{"text":"Family Law"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop the ability to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Read legislation"},{"text":"Understand legal principles"},{"text":"Analyse judgments"},{"text":"Identify legal issues"},{"text":"Prepare case briefs"},{"text":"Write legal arguments"}]}]},{"heading":"Year 2 — Criminal Law Foundation","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is the most important stage for a future prosecutor."},{"type":"h","text":"Criminal Law"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"General principles of criminal liability"},{"text":"Offences against persons"},{"text":"Offences against property"},{"text":"Public-order offences"},{"text":"Economic offences"},{"text":"Cyber offences"},{"text":"Organised crime concepts"},{"text":"Defences and exceptions"},{"text":"Attempt"},{"text":"Abetment"},{"text":"Criminal conspiracy"},{"text":"Joint liability"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Students should study the currently applicable criminal statutes and procedural framework, including the post-2024 Indian criminal-law framework where relevant."},{"type":"h","text":"Criminal Procedure"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"FIR"},{"text":"Investigation"},{"text":"Arrest"},{"text":"Bail"},{"text":"Remand"},{"text":"Charge"},{"text":"Trial"},{"text":"Summons"},{"text":"Warrants"},{"text":"Discharge"},{"text":"Framing of charges"},{"text":"Examination of witnesses"},{"text":"Judgment"},{"text":"Appeal"},{"text":"Revision"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Evidence & Criminal Litigation"},{"type":"h","text":"Evidence"},{"type":"p","text":"A prosecutor must understand how evidence is collected, presented and challenged."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Relevance"},{"text":"Admissibility"},{"text":"Oral evidence"},{"text":"Documentary evidence"},{"text":"Electronic evidence"},{"text":"Expert evidence"},{"text":"Confessions"},{"text":"Admissions"},{"text":"Burden of proof"},{"text":"Presumptions"},{"text":"Witness credibility"},{"text":"Examination and cross-examination"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Criminal Litigation"},{"type":"p","text":"Practice:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Bail arguments"},{"text":"Remand-related submissions"},{"text":"Charge arguments"},{"text":"Witness examination"},{"text":"Cross-examination"},{"text":"Final arguments"},{"text":"Written submissions"},{"text":"Case-law research"}]}]},{"heading":"Final Year — Professional Courtroom Preparation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The final year should focus on applying criminal law to realistic cases."},{"type":"h","text":"Major Areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Trial advocacy"},{"text":"Criminal drafting"},{"text":"Evidence appreciation"},{"text":"Case strategy"},{"text":"Witness examination"},{"text":"Courtroom etiquette"},{"text":"Legal research"},{"text":"Judgment analysis"},{"text":"Ethics"},{"text":"Professional responsibility"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical Exercises"},{"type":"p","text":"Students should conduct mock:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Bail hearings"},{"text":"Trial proceedings"},{"text":"Cross-examinations"},{"text":"Final arguments"},{"text":"Criminal appeals"},{"text":"Evidence objections"}]}]},{"heading":"Core Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Skill Area","Required Skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"Criminal Law"},{"text":"Substantive criminal law"}],[{"text":"Criminal Procedure"},{"text":"Investigation-to-trial process"}],[{"text":"Evidence"},{"text":"Admissibility and appreciation"}],[{"text":"Advocacy"},{"text":"Oral arguments and examination"}],[{"text":"Legal Research"},{"text":"Statutes and case law"}],[{"text":"Drafting"},{"text":"Applications, arguments, submissions"}],[{"text":"Case Analysis"},{"text":"Facts, issues, evidence, law"}],[{"text":"Witness Handling"},{"text":"Examination and cross-examination"}],[{"text":"Courtroom Skills"},{"text":"Procedure, etiquette, advocacy"}],[{"text":"Ethics"},{"text":"Fair prosecution and professional conduct"}],[{"text":"Investigation Awareness"},{"text":"Police investigation process"}],[{"text":"Digital Evidence"},{"text":"Electronic and cyber evidence"}],[{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Clear legal argument"}],[{"text":"Public Service"},{"text":"Government/legal-system orientation"}]]}]},{"heading":"Public Prosecutor Case Workflow","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Criminal Case","Police Investigation","Case Records / Charge-Sheet","Prosecutor Reviews Material","Legal & Evidentiary Analysis","Court Proceedings","Charge / Trial Stage","Prosecution Evidence","Examination of Witnesses","Cross-Examination","Defence Evidence / Submissions","Final Arguments","Judgment","Appeal / Further Proceedings if Applicable"]},{"type":"p","text":"A prosecutor's responsibility is not simply to obtain convictions. The role involves conducting prosecution fairly, presenting relevant evidence and assisting the court in accordance with law and professional duties."}]},{"heading":"Criminal Case Analysis","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong prosecutor should be able to break a case into:"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Facts"},{"type":"p","text":"What actually happened?"},{"type":"h","text":"2. Legal Issues"},{"type":"p","text":"Which offences or legal questions arise?"},{"type":"h","text":"3. Applicable Law"},{"type":"p","text":"Which statutory provisions apply?"},{"type":"h","text":"4. Evidence"},{"type":"p","text":"What evidence supports each relevant fact?"},{"type":"h","text":"5. Witnesses"},{"type":"p","text":"Which witnesses establish which elements?"},{"type":"h","text":"6. Defences"},{"type":"p","text":"What arguments may be raised by the accused?"},{"type":"h","text":"7. Case Theory"},{"type":"p","text":"How does the evidence collectively establish the prosecution's case?"}]},{"heading":"Evidence Analysis Framework","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Alleged Offence","Elements of Offence","Required Facts","Available Evidence","Witnesses","Documents","Electronic / Forensic Evidence","Reliability & Admissibility","Legal Analysis","Court Presentation"]},{"type":"p","text":"The student should learn to distinguish between:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Evidence that exists"},{"text":"Evidence that is legally admissible"},{"text":"Evidence that is reliable"},{"text":"Evidence that actually proves a particular element"}]}]},{"heading":"Witness Examination Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Examination-in-Chief"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Establish witness identity"},{"text":"Establish relevant facts"},{"text":"Build chronological narrative"},{"text":"Introduce relevant evidence"},{"text":"Avoid improper questioning"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cross-Examination"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop skills in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Testing credibility"},{"text":"Identifying inconsistencies"},{"text":"Challenging testimony"},{"text":"Testing perception and memory"},{"text":"Establishing contradictions"},{"text":"Controlling questioning"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Re-Examination"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand when clarification may be necessary following cross-examination."}]},{"heading":"Legal Research Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A prosecutor must be highly comfortable with legal research."},{"type":"h","text":"Research Sources"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Criminal statutes"},{"text":"Procedural laws"},{"text":"Evidence legislation"},{"text":"Constitutional provisions"},{"text":"Supreme Court judgments"},{"text":"High Court judgments"},{"text":"Government notifications"},{"text":"Rules and regulations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research Workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Legal Issue","Identify Relevant Statute","Find Leading Judgments","Check Current Legal Position","Compare Facts","Extract Legal Principle","Apply to Case","Prepare Argument"]},{"type":"p","text":"Students should always verify whether a judgment or statutory provision remains current."}]},{"heading":"Criminal Drafting","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Students should practise drafting:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Bail objections"},{"text":"Written submissions"},{"text":"Legal opinions"},{"text":"Applications"},{"text":"Replies"},{"text":"Criminal complaints"},{"text":"Appeals"},{"text":"Revision-related documents"},{"text":"Case summaries"},{"text":"Arguments"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Drafting should be:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Precise"},{"text":"Evidence-based"},{"text":"Legally supported"},{"text":"Concise"},{"text":"Structured"},{"text":"Professionally formatted"}]}]},{"heading":"Internship Strategy","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For this career, courtroom exposure is extremely valuable."},{"type":"h","text":"Best Internship Environments"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"District courts"},{"text":"High Courts"},{"text":"Criminal law chambers"},{"text":"Public prosecution offices"},{"text":"Government law departments"},{"text":"Legal aid organizations"},{"text":"Criminal litigation practices"},{"text":"Judicial/legal research institutions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Internship Roles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Criminal Law Intern"},{"text":"Litigation Intern"},{"text":"Legal Research Intern"},{"text":"Prosecutor's Office Intern"},{"text":"Court Intern"},{"text":"Legal Aid Intern"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Ideal Progression"},{"type":"flow","items":["Court Observation","Criminal Law Internship","Drafting Practice","Courtroom Assistance","Criminal Litigation Exposure","Independent Advocacy Experience"]}]},{"heading":"Projects During LLB","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Mock Criminal Trial"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a complete simulated criminal trial involving:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"FIR"},{"text":"Investigation"},{"text":"Charge"},{"text":"Witness statements"},{"text":"Documentary evidence"},{"text":"Expert evidence"},{"text":"Examination-in-chief"},{"text":"Cross-examination"},{"text":"Final arguments"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Case-Law Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Select an important criminal judgment and analyse:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Facts"},{"text":"Issues"},{"text":"Statutory provisions"},{"text":"Arguments"},{"text":"Court reasoning"},{"text":"Final decision"},{"text":"Legal significance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Evidence Matrix"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a structured evidence table:"},{"type":"table","header":["Issue","Evidence","Witness","Document","Legal Relevance"],"rows":[[{"text":"Fact 1"},{"text":"Evidence A"},{"text":"Witness 1"},{"text":"Document A"},{"text":"Relevant"}],[{"text":"Fact 2"},{"text":"Evidence B"},{"text":"Witness 2"},{"text":"Document B"},{"text":"Relevant"}],[{"text":"Fact 3"},{"text":"Evidence C"},{"text":"Expert"},{"text":"Report"},{"text":"Requires analysis"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Use fictional/synthetic case data for portfolio work."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Criminal Procedure Flowchart"},{"type":"p","text":"Build an end-to-end criminal case map from:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Complaint/FIR","Investigation","Charge-sheet","Cognizance","Trial","Judgment","Appeal"]}]},{"heading":"Technology Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Modern prosecution increasingly involves digital records and electronic evidence."},{"type":"h","text":"Essential Digital Skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MS Word"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"PDF/document management"},{"text":"Legal databases"},{"text":"Digital case records"},{"text":"Online court systems"},{"text":"Legal research platforms"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging Skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Electronic evidence analysis"},{"text":"Cybercrime fundamentals"},{"text":"Digital forensics awareness"},{"text":"AI-assisted legal research"},{"text":"Legal document management"},{"text":"Case-law analytics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A prosecutor does not need to become a forensic programmer, but should understand how digital evidence is generated, preserved, authenticated and presented."}]},{"heading":"Employer / Recruitment Environment","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Environment","Relevant Skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"Public Prosecution Department"},{"text":"Criminal law, advocacy, procedure"}],[{"text":"Government Law Department"},{"text":"Legal research, drafting"}],[{"text":"District Courts"},{"text":"Trial advocacy, evidence"}],[{"text":"High Courts"},{"text":"Advanced legal research and arguments"}],[{"text":"Legal Aid"},{"text":"Criminal procedure, client interaction"}],[{"text":"Investigative Agencies"},{"text":"Criminal law + evidence awareness"}],[{"text":"Government Legal Cells"},{"text":"Advisory + litigation"}],[{"text":"Judicial/Legal Research"},{"text":"Case analysis, legal writing"}]]}]},{"heading":"Recruitment & Eligibility Preparation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is an important part of the roadmap because “via exams” does not mean one single nationwide Public Prosecutor examination."},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the post and jurisdiction, recruitment may involve:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Competitive examinations"},{"text":"Government recruitment notifications"},{"text":"Eligibility based on legal practice"},{"text":"Interview/selection processes"},{"text":"Experience requirements"},{"text":"Appointment by the competent authority"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Therefore, students should monitor the current official recruitment notification for the relevant State/Central prosecution service."},{"type":"h","text":"Preparation Areas"},{"type":"p","text":"Criminal Law"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Criminal Procedure"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Evidence"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Constitutional Law"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"General Legal Knowledge"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Current Legal Developments"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Legal Drafting"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Case Law"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Language / General Studies"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Interview Preparation"},{"type":"p","text":"The exact syllabus should always be based on the notification for the specific post."}]},{"heading":"Additional Learning & Certifications","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Useful supplementary areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Criminal law"},{"text":"Criminal procedure"},{"text":"Evidence law"},{"text":"Trial advocacy"},{"text":"Legal drafting"},{"text":"Cybercrime"},{"text":"Digital evidence"},{"text":"Forensic science fundamentals"},{"text":"Human rights law"},{"text":"Constitutional law"},{"text":"Legal research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Moot Court"},{"type":"p","text":"Participation in criminal-law moot courts can significantly improve:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Oral advocacy"},{"text":"Legal research"},{"text":"Rebuttal"},{"text":"Case preparation"},{"text":"Courtroom confidence"}]}]},{"heading":"PG Options","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After LLB, possible postgraduate directions include:"},{"type":"p","text":"LL.M."},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Criminal Law"},{"text":"Criminal Justice"},{"text":"Constitutional Law"},{"text":"Human Rights"},{"text":"Cyber Law"},{"text":"Forensic Law"},{"text":"Public Law"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Related Fields"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Criminology"},{"text":"Criminal Justice"},{"text":"Forensic Science"},{"text":"Cybersecurity"},{"text":"Public Policy"},{"text":"Human Rights"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A PG degree can strengthen specialization but does not substitute for any mandatory professional practice or recruitment requirements."}]},{"heading":"Career Specializations","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"1. Trial Prosecutor"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Criminal trials"},{"text":"Witness examination"},{"text":"Evidence"},{"text":"Courtroom advocacy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2. Cybercrime Prosecutor"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cyber offences"},{"text":"Electronic evidence"},{"text":"Digital forensics"},{"text":"Technology law"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3. Economic Offence Prosecutor"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Financial crimes"},{"text":"Fraud"},{"text":"Money laundering-related matters"},{"text":"Corporate offences"}]},{"type":"h","text":"4. Special Criminal Courts"},{"type":"p","text":"Work may involve specialized statutory offences depending on the applicable jurisdiction."},{"type":"h","text":"5. Appeals & Legal Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Criminal appeals"},{"text":"Revision matters"},{"text":"Constitutional/legal questions"},{"text":"Case-law research"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["LLB","Legal Internship","Professional Enrollment / Qualification","Criminal Litigation Experience","Eligibility for Prosecution Recruitment","Assistant / Entry-Level Prosecution Role","Public Prosecutor","Senior Public Prosecutor","Senior Government Law / Prosecution Role","Leadership in Prosecution Administration"]},{"type":"p","text":"Actual progression depends on the recruitment system, seniority, vacancies, experience and applicable government rules."}]},{"heading":"Emerging Technologies","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"AI-Assisted Legal Research"},{"type":"p","text":"AI can assist with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Case-law discovery"},{"text":"Case summarization"},{"text":"Legal issue identification"},{"text":"Document organization"},{"text":"Research drafting"}]},{"type":"p","text":"All outputs require verification against authoritative legal sources."},{"type":"h","text":"Digital Evidence"},{"type":"p","text":"Future prosecutors increasingly need awareness of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mobile-device evidence"},{"text":"CCTV"},{"text":"Metadata"},{"text":"Emails"},{"text":"Digital communications"},{"text":"Cloud records"},{"text":"Social-media evidence"},{"text":"Cybercrime evidence"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Forensic Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"Awareness of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"DNA evidence"},{"text":"Ballistics"},{"text":"Digital forensics"},{"text":"Forensic toxicology"},{"text":"Cyber forensics"},{"text":"Audio/video forensics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"can improve evidence comprehension."}]},{"heading":"Target Profile at Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong candidate should graduate with:"},{"type":"h","text":"Legal Knowledge"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Criminal law"},{"text":"Criminal procedure"},{"text":"Evidence"},{"text":"Constitutional law"},{"text":"Civil procedure"},{"text":"Contract law"},{"text":"Human rights"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advocacy"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Oral arguments"},{"text":"Examination-in-chief"},{"text":"Cross-examination"},{"text":"Rebuttal"},{"text":"Courtroom etiquette"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Statutory research"},{"text":"Case-law research"},{"text":"Judgment analysis"},{"text":"Legal writing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical Experience"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Criminal litigation internship"},{"text":"Court observation"},{"text":"Moot courts"},{"text":"Mock trials"},{"text":"Legal drafting"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Modern Skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Electronic evidence awareness"},{"text":"Cybercrime fundamentals"},{"text":"Legal databases"},{"text":"Digital case management"},{"text":"AI-assisted research with verification"}]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"LLB – Criminal Law"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Criminal Law"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Criminal Procedure"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Evidence"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Trial Advocacy"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Witness Examination"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Legal Research"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Legal Drafting"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Courtroom Practice"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Forensic Evidence Awareness"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Digital Evidence"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Constitutional Law"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Professional Ethics"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Criminal Litigation Experience"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Recruitment Examination Preparation"}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["LLB","Criminal Law Specialization","Criminal Litigation Internships","Professional Enrollment/Qualification","Criminal Practice","Required Experience","Prosecution Recruitment/Appointment","Public Prosecutor","Senior Prosecution Role"]},{"type":"p","text":"For the database, the most important qualification note is:"},{"type":"p","text":"Public Prosecutor is a regulated government/legal role. An LLB is the educational foundation, but appointment is subject to the applicable jurisdiction's eligibility, professional-practice requirements, recruitment process and government notification."}]}]}